[{"data":1,"prerenderedAt":121},["ShallowReactive",2],{"/gis/store-dataset":3,"/gis/store-dataset-surround":110},{"id":4,"title":5,"body":6,"description":75,"extension":76,"meta":77,"navigation":95,"path":106,"seo":107,"stem":108,"__hash__":109},"content/gis/store-dataset.md","GIS Extension Dictionary: store-dataset",{"type":7,"value":8,"toc":64},"minimark",[9],[10,11,15,16,15,26,51,55,58,61],"div",{"className":12,"id":14},[13],"dict_entry","store-dataset","\n  ",[17,18,20,21,15],"h3",{"id":19},"gisstore-dataset","\n    ",[22,23,25],"a",{"href":24},"#store-dataset","gis:store-dataset",[27,28,32],"h4",{"id":29,"className":30},"gisstore-dataset-dataset-file",[31],"section-heading",[22,33,20,37,15],{"className":34,"href":36},[35],"section-anchor","#----gisstore-dataset-dataset-file--",[38,39,42,43,47,48],"span",{"className":40},[41],"prim_example","gis:store-dataset ",[44,45,46],"i",{},"dataset"," ",[44,49,50],{},"file",[52,53,54],"p",{},"Exports the given dataset to the given file.",[52,56,57],{},"For VectorDatasets, two file formats are supported, ESRI shapefiles\nand GeoJSON. If the given file name ends in “.geojson” or “.json”,\nthen the file will be exported as a GeoJSON file. If the file name\nends in any other extension or no extension at all, the dataset\nwill be exported as a shapefile and the associated file extensions\nwill be supplied (“.shp”, “.prj”, etc.)",[52,59,60],{},"For RasterDatasets, only ESRI ASCII grid files are supported and\nthe associated file extensions will be automatically supplied.",[52,62,63],{},"Relative paths are resolved relative to the location of the current\nmodel, or the user’s home directory if the current model hasn’t\nbeen saved yet.",{"title":65,"searchDepth":66,"depth":67,"links":68},"",5,3,[69],{"id":19,"depth":67,"text":70,"children":71},"\n    gis:store-dataset\n  ",[72],{"id":29,"depth":73,"text":74},4,"\n    gis:store-dataset dataset file\n  ","Documentation for the store-dataset primitive.","md",{"source":78,"metadataOut